Rewritten: the provider profile itself (its default base of
http://127.0.0.1:9376/v1, its placeholder key variable, its curated fallback
model list, and its chat-completions wire) as a Nodecode catalog row, a
credential hook and one request-body hook; and the reasoning-effort clamp,
which reads the local proxy's own GET /models catalog for each model's
reasoning.supported and reasoning.allowed_efforts and never sends a level a
serving node did not declare.

Left out, and why: Hermes' private seams the original imported
(agent.reasoning_effort, providers.base, hermes_cli.urllib_security) have no
place here, so the effort ladder is Nodecode's own -- which spells the
disabled tier `off' and always offers it, where Hermes had `none' only where a
node declared it (the hook still says `none' on the wire for a node that
declares it). The original's synchronous cold-cache seed with a 2-second
timeout and its 30-second post-failure backoff become one bounded read at
start plus a worker that asks again every five minutes, keeping the last map
through a failure; and its per-provider default auxiliary model has no
per-provider home in Nodecode, so it is not carried over.
